    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d665">

                <pb facs="0692" n="642" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg642"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Grip.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-25"><hi rendition="#italic">August 25,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to apprise you, in
                    connection with previous correspondence upon the subject, of the receipt of a
                    telegram from the Acting Secretary of the Treasury of the 23d instant, saying
                    that the Treasury Department has issued instructions to the collectors of
                    customs at the principal ports to receive certificates of admeasurement of
                    vessels of Norway, as expressed in registers granted prior to royal decree of
                    September 14, 1893, and therefore under the old rule.</p>
                <p>Mr. Wike adds that your further requests are under consideration and that they
                    will be disposed of at an early date.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
